A sandboxed file interface over Linux file descriptors.

Use alloc, core, io, and string.

A public record File has an fd as a whole number.

To open_file given path as a pointer to TcString, flags as a whole number, returning Result of File and whole number.
    Define local descriptor as a whole number.
    Set descriptor to ask Linux kernel 257 with -100, path.data, flags, and 420.
    Define local answer as Result of File and whole number.
    If descriptor < 0:
        Set answer.is_ok to false.
        Set answer.err_val to descriptor.
        Give back answer.
    Define local handle as File.
    Set handle.fd to descriptor.
    Set answer.is_ok to true.
    Set answer.ok_val to handle.
    Give back answer.
Done.

Publicly, to file_open_read given path as a pointer to TcString, returning Result of File and whole number.
    Give back open_file(path, 0).
Done.

Publicly, to file_open_write given path as a pointer to TcString, returning Result of File and whole number.
    Give back open_file(path, 578).
Done.

Publicly, to file_open_append given path as a pointer to TcString, returning Result of File and whole number.
    Give back open_file(path, 1090).
Done.

Publicly, to file_read_bytes given f as a pointer to File, buf as a pointer to byte, max_len as an unsigned number, returning a whole number.
    Give back ask Linux kernel 0 with f.fd, buf, and max_len.
Done.

Publicly, to file_write_bytes given f as a pointer to File, buf as a pointer to byte, len as an unsigned number, returning a whole number.
    Give back ask Linux kernel 1 with f.fd, buf, and len.
Done.

Publicly, to file_seek given f as a pointer to File, offset as a whole number, whence as a whole number, returning a whole number.
    Give back ask Linux kernel 8 with f.fd, offset, and whence.
Done.

Publicly, to file_close given f as a pointer to File, returning a whole number.
    Define local result as a whole number.
    Set result to ask Linux kernel 3 with f.fd.
    Set f.fd to -1.
    Give back result.
Done.

Publicly, to write_str_to_file given s as a pointer to TcString, path as a pointer to TcString, returning a whole number.
    Call this as "save <s> to file <path>".
    Define local opened as Result of File and whole number.
    Set opened to file_open_write(path).
    If not opened.is_ok:
        Give back opened.err_val.
    Define local handle as File.
    Set handle to opened.ok_val.
    Define local written as a whole number.
    Set written to file_write_bytes(address of handle, s.data, s.len).
    file_close(address of handle).
    Give back written.
Done.

Publicly, to write_i64_to_file given n as a whole number, path as a pointer to TcString, returning a whole number.
    Call this as "save <n> to file <path>".
    Define local buffer as block of 32 byte.
    Define local len as an unsigned number.
    Set len to format_i64_into(n, address of item 0 of buffer).
    Define local opened as Result of File and whole number.
    Set opened to file_open_write(path).
    If not opened.is_ok:
        Give back opened.err_val.
    Define local handle as File.
    Set handle to opened.ok_val.
    Define local written as a whole number.
    Set written to file_write_bytes(address of handle, address of item 0 of buffer, len).
    file_close(address of handle).
    Give back written.
Done.

Publicly, to write_f64_to_file given x as a decimal, path as a pointer to TcString, returning a whole number.
    Call this as "save <x> to file <path>".
    Define local buffer as block of 64 byte.
    Define local len as an unsigned number.
    Set len to format_f64_into(x, address of item 0 of buffer).
    Define local opened as Result of File and whole number.
    Set opened to file_open_write(path).
    If not opened.is_ok:
        Give back opened.err_val.
    Define local handle as File.
    Set handle to opened.ok_val.
    Define local written as a whole number.
    Set written to file_write_bytes(address of handle, address of item 0 of buffer, len).
    file_close(address of handle).
    Give back written.
Done.

Publicly, to read_file_to_str given path as a pointer to TcString, returning Result of TcString and whole number.
    Define local answer as Result of TcString and whole number.
    Define local opened as Result of File and whole number.
    Set opened to file_open_read(path).
    If not opened.is_ok:
        Set answer.is_ok to false.
        Set answer.err_val to opened.err_val.
        Give back answer.
    Define local handle as File.
    Set handle to opened.ok_val.
    Define local size as a whole number.
    Set size to file_seek(address of handle, 0, 2).
    If size < 0:
        file_close(address of handle).
        Set answer.is_ok to false.
        Set answer.err_val to -5.
        Give back answer.
    file_seek(address of handle, 0, 0).
    Define local text as TcString.
    Set text.len to size as an unsigned number.
    Set text.cap to text.len + 1.
    Set text.data to heap_alloc(text.cap).
    Define local read_count as a whole number.
    Set read_count to file_read_bytes(address of handle, text.data, text.len).
    If read_count < 0:
        file_close(address of handle).
        heap_free(text.data).
        Set answer.is_ok to false.
        Set answer.err_val to -5.
        Give back answer.
    Set text.len to read_count as an unsigned number.
    Set item text.len of text.data to 0.
    file_close(address of handle).
    Set answer.is_ok to true.
    Set answer.ok_val to text.
    Give back answer.
Done.

Publicly, to display_file given path as a pointer to TcString, returning a whole number.
    Call this as "display file <path>".
    Define local opened as Result of TcString and whole number.
    Set opened to read_file_to_str(path).
    If not opened.is_ok:
        Give back opened.err_val.
    Define local text as TcString.
    Set text to opened.ok_val.
    If text.len > 0:
        Ask Linux kernel 1 with 1, text.data, and text.len.
    Ask Linux kernel 1 with 1, "\n", and 1.
    Define local length as a whole number.
    Set length to text.len as a whole number.
    str_free(address of text).
    Give back length.
Done.

Publicly, to file_exists given path as a pointer to TcString, returning a truth value.
    Call this as "file exists <path>".
    Define local opened as Result of File and whole number.
    Set opened to file_open_read(path).
    If not opened.is_ok:
        Give back false.
    Define local handle as File.
    Set handle to opened.ok_val.
    file_close(address of handle).
    Give back true.
Done.

Publicly, to delete_file given path as a pointer to TcString, returning a whole number.
    Call this as "delete file <path>".
    Call this as "remove file <path>".
    Give back ask Linux kernel 263 with -100, path.data, and 0.
Done.
